body:
I'm implementing instantsearch.js in vanilla JavaScript in a way very similar to the e-commerce (2nd) example in https://community.algolia.com/instantsearch.js/v1/examples/

When it works, it works brilliantly. But often when I click in the search bar nothing happens. I must reload the page a few times and wait. Usually then somehow instantsearch begins to work.

I thought maybe it was a promise issue so I implemented that (see code below). This seems to have no effect however.
```
            window.onload = function() {
                let loadSearchPromise = search.start();
                document.getElementById('search__input').onclick = function() {
                    loadSearchPromise.then(() => {
                      document.getElementById('show-result').style.display = 'block';
                    })
                }
            }
```
It's frustrating when clicking in the search bar and reloading the first few times doesn't work, so I have some general questions:
- What could be causing this delay, and if so what can be done about it?
- Does a promise implementation for instantsearch.js make sense?

There are no slow network issues on my end.
